{
  "id": "queue-kanji-lead-deck-limit",
  "title": "A capped deck's lead ends with the kanji that uses up its limit: a kanji homed elsewhere is not shown and then withdrawn (C-28d)",
  "covers": [
    "queue.kanji_lead_deck_limit"
  ],
  "narrative": [
    "The deck 'Core' has new_cards_per_day 1 and holds, in position order, the new word 学校 (card ...10) and the new kanji note 学 (card ...20). The new kanji note 校 (card ...30) is an item of the disabled deck 'Kanji' only, so it has no turn of its own. The global goal is the default 20; nothing is due.",
    "Step 0: the unit [学, 校, 学校] has deck cost 2 (the word and 学, homed in 'Core'), more than the deck's remaining 1, so it leads. 学 fits and uses up the limit, and the lead ends there (QueueBuilder rule 4 'Lead', 'The lead ends at the deck's limit'): 校 is not served although its deck cost is 0. Only 学 is served; until_stop is 1. Before C-28d the build was [学, 校] and 校 vanished after 学 was answered (until_stop 2, then 0).",
    "Step 1 answers 学 Easy. Step 2: the deck's limit is used up: no item, until_stop 0. Nothing that step 0 showed has disappeared.",
    "Step 3, the next study day (04:00:01Z): 学 is started, the unit is [校, 学校] with deck cost 1, drawn whole: 校, then 学校. until_stop is 2."
  ],
